## a b s t r a c t
The fabrication of efficient bi-functional catalysts for oxygen reduction reaction (ORR) and oxygen evolution reaction (OER) applied in energy storage and conversion devices like Zn-air batteries to solve the growing energy and environmental crises has attracted great attentions. In this work, the Fe$\mathsf{C e@G S L}$ catalysts have developed by first constructing the MOF/LDH/GO templates with multi-stage mixed growth method followed by calcining the template at high temperature. Fe-Ni-LDH (hydrotalcite) plays the role of linking the metal organic frameworks (Fe-Ce-MOF) and graphene oxides (GO), avoiding the separation of MOFs derivatives and GO sheets during pyrolysis process. Rare-earth metal oxide $(\mathsf{C e O}_{2})$ featuring with abundant oxygen vacancies dispersed on the surface of transition-metal oxide can efficiently improve the stability of catalysts. The optimal $\mathrm{Fe}_{7}–\mathrm{Ce}_{1}@\mathrm{GSL}–800$ catalysts exhibit excellent ORR/OER performances with the potential gap between ORR $\mathrm{(E_{1/2}}=0.87\:\mathrm{V}$ ) and OER $(\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{J}=10}=1.59\:\mathrm{V})$ of $0.720\mathrm{V}.$ . The aqueous $Z\mathrm{n}$ -air battery assembled with $\mathrm{Fe}_{7^{-}}\mathrm{Ce}_{1}@\mathrm{GSL}–800$ catalysts exhibits outstanding performances with high open circuit voltage $(1.56\mathrm{V})$ , large specific capacity $(801.1\ \mathrm{mAh/g@10\\mathrm{mA.cm^{-2}}})$ , and good charge–discharge cycle performances $(>500\ \mathrm{h}),$ . The $\mathrm{Fe}_{7^{-}}\mathrm{Ce}_{1}@\mathrm{GSL}–800$ based solid-state Zn-air battery also delivers an excellent performance with high specific capacity $(791.7~\mathrm{mAh}/\mathrm{g}@5~\mathrm{mA.cm}^{-2})$ and long cycle stability $\left(>230\mathrm{h}\right)$ .
